# CMS Admin Razor Patterns

Follow `cms-admin-design-system` for look and RTL. This rule covers structure and MVC patterns.

## Structure

```
CMS.Web/Areas/Admin/
├── Controllers/
├── Views/
│   ├── Shared/
│   │   ├── _AdminLayout.cshtml
│   │   ├── _Sidebar.cshtml
│   │   └── _ValidationScriptsPartial.cshtml
│   └── {Feature}/
└── ViewModels/
```

Module admin UI lives under `CMS.Modules/{Module}/Web/Areas/Admin/` and registers into the same Admin area.

## Layout

- One `_AdminLayout.cshtml` with `lang="fa"` `dir="rtl"`.
- Views set `Layout = "_AdminLayout"`.
- Shared chrome (sidebar, top bar, flash, **filter panel**) only in Shared partials — never copy into feature views.
- List Index toolbars use `<partial name="_FilterPanel" />` (see `cms-admin-filters`).

## Controllers

- Thin: bind → authorize → call Application → map to ViewModel → return View/Redirect.
- Prefer `XxxViewModel` over entities/DTOs in views.
- Use `[Area("Admin")]` and `[Authorize]` on all admin controllers.
- PRG after POST: redirect with TempData flash; do not re-render success on POST.

## Forms

- Always include antiforgery (`asp-antiforgery` / `@Html.AntiForgeryToken()`).
- Label above field; validation message below; Persian copy via localizer.
- One primary submit button per form; cancel is secondary link/button.
- Prefer tag helpers (`asp-for`, `asp-action`, `asp-controller`).

```cshtml
<form asp-action="Create" method="post">
  <div asp-validation-summary="ModelOnly"></div>
  <label asp-for="Title"></label>
  <input asp-for="Title" />
  <span asp-validation-for="Title"></span>
  <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">ذخیره</button>
</form>
```

## Flash & Empty States

- Success/error via `TempData["Success"]` / `TempData["Error"]` rendered once in layout.
- Empty lists: short Persian message + one primary CTA (e.g. ایجاد).

## Do Not

- Put business logic or EF queries in views or controllers.
- Use English-only labels/placeholders in admin UI.
- Inline one-off CSS that fights the design system — extend admin CSS instead.
